 NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS="--threads 4" APEX_PARALLEL_BUILD=8 APEX_CPP_EXT=1 APEX_CUDA_EXT=1 pip install -v --no-build-isolation .
 ```
 
+If the CUDA-compatible compiler used for toolkit version detection is not
+located at `$CUDA_HOME/bin/nvcc`, set `APEX_NVCC` to its executable path:
+
+```bash
+APEX_NVCC=/path/to/nvcc APEX_CPP_EXT=1 APEX_CUDA_EXT=1 pip install -v --no-build-isolation .
+```
+
+`CUDA_HOME` continues to control the toolkit include and library paths.
+
 When CPU cores or memory are limited, the `--parallel` option is generally preferred over `--threads`. See [pull#1882](https://github.com/NVIDIA/apex/pull/1882) for more details.
 
